user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 29,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_direct_counterargument",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Other users' comments in OC_comments, read against the OP title/argument: 1 if any comment directly counterargues the OP's stated view, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title, argument and every comment in the OC_comments JSON list together. Return 1 if at least one comment directly counterargues the OP's view: it explicitly opposes, rebuts, or gives reasons or evidence against a specific claim or conclusion in the title/argument. Return 0 if all comments are assessable and none do so (e.g. only questions, clarification requests, agreement, jokes, off-topic, moderator/bot notices). Do not use the conversation column or any later replies. Quoted text from others does not count unless the comment itself rebuts it. Return null if OC_comments is missing, unparseable or empty, or if title and argument are both missing."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 37,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_contrasts_op_view_with_personal_experience",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments, other users): 1 if any comment explicitly contrasts the OP's view with a relatable real-world personal experience of the commenter or someone they personally know, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title and argument (OP view/target) and the OC_comments JSON list (comments by users other than OP; order carries no meaning) jointly. Return 1 if at least one comment recounts a real-world personal experience (the commenter's own or that of someone they personally know, e.g. family/friends; not hypotheticals, generic statistics, news, historical or public-figure examples) AND explicitly sets it against the OP's stated view, i.e. uses it to show the view does not match, hold or apply in that experience. The experience should be relatable (ordinary everyday life, not purely technical/abstract). Experience merely mentioned without being contrasted with the OP's view gives 0. Do not use the conversation column or later replies; ignore quoted text by third parties unless adopted. Return 0 if all comments are assessable and none qualify. Return null if OC_comments is missing, unparseable, or title/argument missing so the OP view cannot be identified. An empty list gives 0."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
